  "id": "ex-19-indirekte-rede-b2",
  "intro": "Standalone drill set, not tied to any lesson. Formal written German reports what someone said using Konjunktiv I, not just \"dass\" + Indikativ: Er sagt, er SEI müde (not: er ist müde) — it signals \"this is a claim, not a fact I'm vouching for,\" which is exactly why newspapers use it. sein is fully irregular (sei, seist, sei, seien, seiet, seien); most other verbs just add -e to the stem for er/sie/es: er habe, er komme, er gehe, er könne, er müsse. This set sticks to the common, unambiguous 3rd-person-singular case. Blocks: A Basistraining → B Vertiefung → C Sprachbausteine → D Wiederholung. Answers in solutions.md.\n",
  "lesson": "EX/19-indirekte-rede-b2",
  "level": "B2",
  "summary": null,
  "title": "Indirekte Rede: Konjunktiv I — B2",
